WEBVTT

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:07.540
Thanks for tuning into Planet Terry Dash Daily, episode 56 for May 6th, 2026.

00:00:08.380 --> 00:00:10.400
Let's see what the latest research is telling us.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:17.560
A single 25 milligram dose of psilocybin produced measurable brain structural changes in healthy

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:20.800
adults that persisted for at least one month.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.160
Across over study of 28 healthy volunteers with no prior psychedelic experience showed this

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:29.140
outcome clearly.

00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:36.160
The 25 milligram dose created detectable shifts in brain structure at the one month mark according

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.320
to imaging results.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.920
The one milligram control dose produced no comparable structural changes.

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:50.220
These findings identify a concrete window for studying how brief pharmacological interventions

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:52.760
can influence adult neural architecture.

00:00:53.760 --> 00:00:58.600
The changes appeared without any previous psychedelic exposure in the participants.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:05.580
psilocybin produced clear structural shifts visible on imaging one month later distinct

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.040
from the minimal effects of the lower dose.

00:01:08.920 --> 00:01:14.980
This opens a window into how brief interventions might influence neural connectivity in adults

00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:18.600
with possible relevance for mood and cognitive disorders.

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:24.400
Larger trials will still be needed to connect these structural observations to functional

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:25.660
or clinical outcomes.

00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:32.720
Most people assume the brain's basic wiring is finished by early adulthood and changes little

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:33.360
afterward.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:39.360
In reality, the adult brain retains substantial capacity to alter its physical structure

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.680
in response to experience or compounds.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:47.540
Right now as you read this, synaptic connections throughout your cortex are being strengthened

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:52.120
or pruned based on what you pay attention to and what you encounter.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:59.680
A recent study captured one striking example with a single 25 milligram dose of psilocybin

00:01:59.680 --> 00:02:05.220
producing measurable shifts in brain architecture still detectable four weeks later.

00:02:05.760 --> 00:02:11.340
That duration of four weeks of visible change after one exposure illustrates how quickly

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.420
and durably the adult brain can reorganize.

00:02:15.140 --> 00:02:20.520
Every day choices such as learning new skills or managing stress continue to reshape neural

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:23.040
tissue well into later life.

00:02:23.940 --> 00:02:29.660
Future therapies may deliberately harness this ongoing plasticity rather than assuming it

00:02:29.660 --> 00:02:36.800
as ended while targeted compounds can drive measurable brain changes along established behavior

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:39.960
offers even broader effects on disease risk.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:46.300
New evidence synthesis positions regular physical activity as one of the most effective tools

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:49.560
for lowering risk across multiple disease categories.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:56.480
The review underscores that exercise works through overlapping physiological pathways rather

00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.040
than any single mechanism.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:05.000
This multi pathway action helps explain the wide range of benefits observed across cardiovascular,

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.580
metabolic, and neurological health.

00:03:08.580 --> 00:03:15.140
Regular movement influences inflammation, insulin sensitivity, and vascular function simultaneously.

00:03:15.860 --> 00:03:22.820
The synthesis draws together data showing consistent risk reduction even with moderate activity levels.

00:03:23.440 --> 00:03:30.000
These results strengthen recommendations for physical activity as a foundational prevention strategy.

00:03:30.320 --> 00:03:36.840
On a different note, population level prevention also depends on accurate expectations for screening

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:39.040
tools such as colonoscopy.

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:45.680
13-year follow-up data show that colonoscopy delivers measurable but smaller reductions in

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:50.780
colorectal cancer incidence and mortality than earlier models predicted.

00:03:52.440 --> 00:03:57.320
The narrower benefits help refine realistic targets for what population screening programs

00:03:57.320 --> 00:03:58.100
can achieve.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:05.180
Earlier projections may have overstated the population wide impact based on shorter term observations.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:11.180
These longer term results allow planners to adjust resource allocation and communication

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:12.180
around screening.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:19.280
Colonoscopy remains a valuable tool yet its expected yield needs calibration against these findings.

00:04:20.080 --> 00:04:26.800
Shifting focus now to advances in biotechnology where precision at the molecular level is improving.

00:04:27.460 --> 00:04:33.880
Researchers can now reliably construct and insert very large DNA segments including complete

00:04:33.880 --> 00:04:38.820
metabolic pathways and extra chromosomes into yeast and bacteria.

00:04:39.620 --> 00:04:45.000
This capability allows redesign of microbes to produce complex medicines and industrial

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:46.520
chemicals more efficiently.

00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:53.300
The assembled DNA segments function as ready made factories within the host organisms.

00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:59.540
Such advances reduce the time and cost associated with developing new production strains.

00:05:00.540 --> 00:05:06.020
The technology supports both pharmaceutical manufacturing and sustainable chemical synthesis.

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:12.200
Precision at the molecular level also matters for understanding and addressing widespread

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.980
nutritional deficiencies.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:22.960
An analysis spanning 1990 to 2021 quantifies iron deficiency anemia burdens among women

00:05:22.960 --> 00:05:26.100
of child bearing age across regions and nations.

00:05:27.100 --> 00:05:32.760
The detailed geographic patterns supply public health planners with clear targets for intervention.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:39.860
Certain regions show persistently higher rates that correlate with dietary and environmental factors.

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:47.560
Mapping these burdens over three decades reveals both progress in some areas and ongoing challenges in others.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:54.620
The data enable more precise allocation of supplements, education and fortification programs.

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:01.220
Such geographic insights support tailored strategies that address local needs effectively.

00:06:02.080 --> 00:06:08.800
Geographic patterns of disease paired naturally with efforts to find parasites-specific drug-hard targets.

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:15.960
Researchers used PEG-400 to expose a binding pocket on the partial pain to enzyme

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:19.200
that exists only in plasmodium parasites.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:25.660
The discovery provides a route to compounds that disable the parasite while sparing the human

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:32.600
version of the enzyme. This parasite only feature minimizes the risk of off-target effects in human

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:38.900
cells. Structural studies like this accelerate the search for selective inhibitors with improved

00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:45.880
safety profiles. The approach could lead to new classes of antimaloreal agents that exploit

00:06:45.880 --> 00:06:52.700
unique parasite biology. Selective targeting is also being tested in condensed treatment schedules

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:58.460
for certain cancers. A United Kingdom trial found that patients with a specific

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:05.120
core-electural cancer subtype who received nine weeks of pembrolizamab before surgery remained

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:12.080
cancer-free nearly three years later. The short pre-operative immunotherapy course showed durable

00:07:12.080 --> 00:07:18.820
responses in this selected group. These outcomes suggest a condensed regimen may reduce the need

00:07:18.820 --> 00:07:25.440
for prolonged post-operative chemotherapy. Patients could experience fewer long-term side effects

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:31.700
while maintaining cancer control. The results point to opportunities for personalizing treatment

00:07:31.700 --> 00:07:39.020
duration based on tumor characteristics. Less invasive approaches are also advancing in the operating

00:07:39.020 --> 00:07:46.540
room itself. Johnson and Johnson's OTAVA soft tissue surgical robot met its primary safety and

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:54.320
performance endpoints in an initial study of gastric bypass procedures. The data mark an early step

00:07:54.320 --> 00:08:02.380
toward wider use in minimally invasive abdominal surgery. The system demonstrated reliable performance

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:09.340
across the tested cases. Robotic assistance may expand access to precise techniques with reduced

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:15.220
recovery times for patients. Ungoing refinements could integrate this platform into additional

00:08:15.220 --> 00:08:21.780
surgical specialities. These incremental advances across brain biology prevention and precision

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:28.920
tools illustrate steady progress in understanding and supporting human health. Keep an eye on larger

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:35.400
trials that will connect these brain structural observations from psilocybin to specific functional

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:45.220
and clinical outcomes. That's Planet Terrianne daily for today. If you enjoyed this, a rating or review

